Remove the pingsender binary from the build and the package.

pingsender.exe is the standalone helper Firefox uses to transmit telemetry
pings (notably at shutdown, when the main process can't wait on the network).
Upstream builds and packages it UNCONDITIONALLY — even with telemetry
reporting, health report, and Normandy compiled out, the transmitter binary
still ships. Sanctum's principle is that transmission code must not exist in
the binary at all, so drop it from the build DIRS and the package manifest.

The BackgroundTask_pingsender.sys.mjs module it pairs with is inert without
the binary and the (disabled+locked) telemetry callers, so it is left alone
to keep this patch minimal and rebase-friendly.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/telemetry/moz.build b/toolkit/components/telemetry/moz.build
--- a/toolkit/components/telemetry/moz.build
+++ b/toolkit/components/telemetry/moz.build
@@ -7,9 +7,5 @@
 include("/ipc/chromium/chromium-config.mozbuild")

 FINAL_LIBRARY = "xul"

-DIRS = [
-    "pingsender",
-]
-
 if CONFIG["COMPILE_ENVIRONMENT"]:
diff --git a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
--- a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
+++ b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
@@ -397,7 +397,3 @@
 #endif

-; [ Ping Sender ]
-;
-@BINPATH@/pingsender@BIN_SUFFIX@
-
 ; [ Native Messaging Host Proxy ]
